---
description: Tailwind CSS and UI rules
alwaysApply: true
---

## Styling Rules

- Tailwind CSS only.
- Reuse existing utility classes.
- Mobile first.
- Responsive layouts required.
- Keep spacing consistent.
- Prefer clean modern UI.
- Avoid oversized paddings/margins.
- Avoid decorative clutter.
- Preserve existing visual style.

## Admin Panel UI

Priority:
1. information density
2. readability
3. speed of use
4. responsive support

Rules:
- Prefer compact layouts in admin panel.
- Tables may scroll horizontally.
- Controls should be compact.
- Forms should be efficient.
- Desktop-first, mobile supported.
- Actions should be obvious.
- Avoid large empty spaces.
- Avoid oversized cards, paddings, buttons, and inputs unless current project style requires them.

## Modal Rules

- Use portal when existing project pattern uses portal.
- Close on overlay click if current UX allows.
- Prevent body scroll while opened.
- Respect viewport height.
- Internal content should scroll, not the whole page.
- Mobile modal may use bottom-sheet style.
- Desktop modal should be centered.
- Modals must fit viewport height.

## Table Rules

- Tables must be responsive.
- Horizontal scroll is allowed.
- Use compact row height.
- Numeric columns should be aligned right if useful.
- Actions should be aligned consistently.
- Preserve readability on mobile.